---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import PrimaryButton from "../components/buttons/PrimaryButton.astro";
import { readSettings, buildCanonicalUrl } from "../utils/settings";

const settings = readSettings();
const canonical = buildCanonicalUrl(settings, { path: "/about" });
const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "About" },
];
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="About the WitchClick project."
  canon={canonical}
>
  <Breadcrumbs slot="breadcrumbs" items={breadcrumbs} />
  <article class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none space-y-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
      <h1>About WitchClick</h1>
      <p>
        WitchClick is a secular sanctuary for people who crave ritual without rigidity. We blend cozy aesthetics, trauma-aware
        planning, and small acts of wonder so you can reclaim momentum—even on a low-spoon day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here is medical, legal, or therapeutic advice. Take what resonates, adapt every ritual to your bodymind, and
        leave the rest at the altar.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>Brand manifesto</h2>
      <p>
        We believe magic lives in the tiny choices you can actually make. WitchClick celebrates rituals that are slow, consent-
        filled, and accessible. Every guide is an invitation—not a commandment.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Build comfort-first systems that honor neurodivergent rhythms and chronic-illness realities.</li>
        <li>Offer evidence-aware insights while leaving room for wonder, intuition, and play.</li>
        <li>Design with accessibility at the forefront: adjustable themes, friendly fonts, and short summaries.</li>
        <li>Champion rest as productive, boundaries as sacred, and softness as a strategic advantage.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Values we nurture</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Gentle agency.</strong> Your autonomy matters more than any spell. Every ritual comes with choose-your-own-
          pace variations and plain-language safety notes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Inclusive coziness.</strong> We write for queer, neurodivergent, disabled, and multi-faith practitioners who
          want practical enchantment without gatekeeping.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evidence & intuition in dialogue.</strong> Research citations, lived experience, and creative prompts sit
          side-by-side so you can blend head and heart.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transparency.</strong> Affiliate disclosures, data practices, and pricing are plain to find and easy to opt out
          of.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Boundaries we honor</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>No spiritual supremacy.</strong> We do not appropriate closed practices or claim a single “correct” path to
          healing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No productivity shame.</strong> We reject hustle dogma. Rest, collapse, and grief get as much space here as
          glow-up moments.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No purity tests.</strong> You can be skeptical, witchy-curious, or full-on occult nerd—everyone deserves tools
          that meet them where they are.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No exploitation.</strong> Partnerships and recommendations must align with our ethics: fair labor, inclusive
          design, and joyful usefulness.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>If a collaboration or request crosses these lines, we lovingly decline.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="membership" class="space-y-4">
      <h2>Membership &amp; account roadmap</h2>
      <p>
        A dedicated member portal is on the horizon. It will hold bookmarking, ritual tracking, and printable libraries for
        subscribers who want everything in one midnight-bright dashboard. Until the infrastructure is ready, account links point
        you here so expectations stay clear.
      </p>
      <p>
        Want to help shape the rollout? We’re gathering cozy testers who can share accessibility needs, pricing feedback, and
        the rituals you want prioritized.
      </p>
      <PrimaryButton href="/contact" iconAfter="↗">
        Tell us what you need
      </PrimaryButton>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
